===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# Outward appearance.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Sonnets|102|passage=My loue is strengthned though more weake in '''seeming''' <br> I loue not lesse, thogh lesse the show appeare,}}
#* {{RQ:Poe Raven|passage=And his eyes have all the '''seeming''' of a demon’s that is dreaming}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1971|author={{w|Iris Murdoch}}|title={{w|An Accidental Man}}|url=https://archive.org/details/accidentalman00murd|page=162|publisher=Viking|location=New York
|passage=I am not what I seemed to her, he thought, and doubtless she is not what she seemed to me, but it is our lot to be irrevocably condemned to '''seemings''' and to deserve them too.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[apprehension|Apprehension]]; [[judgement]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1604|author={{w|Richard Hooker}}|title=Of the Lawes of Ecclesiasticall Politie|location=London|publisher=Preface|page=39|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A03590.0001.001
|passage=Nothing more cleare vnto their '''seeming''', then that a new Jerusalem being often spoken of in Scripture, they vndoubtedly were themselues that newe Ierusalem,}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|8|lines=736-738|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A50919.0001.001|text={{...}} in her ears the sound<br>Yet rung of his perswasive words, impregn’d<br>With Reason, to her '''seeming''', and with Truth;}}

